WHAT THIS PROJECT IS FOR
------------------------

JobDibs was written so that a person looking for work can search on their own
computer without handing their CV to anyone. Everything runs locally; the only
outbound requests are to public job-board endpoints, made from the user's own
machine.

The AGPL cannot and does not restrict how you use the software. The following
is a statement of intent, not a licence term. Please do not build things that:

  - collect, store or transmit other people's CVs without their knowledge
  - submit applications automatically on someone's behalf without their review
  - scrape sites that prohibit it, including LinkedIn and national job boards
  - present listings as current when they are stale

If you host a modified version for other people, note that section 13 of the
AGPL requires you to offer those users the complete source code of your
version.


